---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../../lib/schema';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy Policy',
    description: 'How Joshua Israel Ventures LLC handles personal data on pickyourrow.com.',
    url: 'https://pickyourrow.com/privacy/',
    publisher: PUBLISHER,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://pickyourrow.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: 'https://pickyourrow.com/privacy/' },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for pickyourrow.com. Joshua Israel Ventures LLC is the data controller. What we collect through the contact form, analytics (including Google Analytics 4) and hosting, and your choices."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</nav>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This policy explains what personal data pickyourrow.com collects, why, and what you can do about it. The short
      version: we collect very little, we do not sell your data, and Google sets cookies to show ads.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated 28 October 2026.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      Pick Your Row is a brand owned and operated by Joshua Israel Ventures LLC. Joshua Israel Ventures LLC is the
      data controller for personal data collected through this site. Contact:
      <a href="mailto:joshuaofisrael@gmail.com">joshuaofisrael@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>When you use the contact form</h3>
    <p>
      The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> asks for your name, email address and message, and optionally a phone
      number. When you press send, your browser submits these details to FormSubmit (formsubmit.co), a third party
      form service, which forwards them to us by email. We receive and store the email in a Google Gmail account. We
      use these details only to read and reply to your message. If you email us directly, we receive the details in
      your email in the same way.
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are useful. Its script reports information
      such as the page you viewed, the referring page, your browser and device type, your approximate country and
      page load timing. Cloudflare says this service does not use cookies or local storage and does not fingerprint
      individual visitors. We see only aggregated statistics. See the
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 id="google-analytics">Google Analytics 4</h3>
    <p>
      If you press Accept on our cookie banner, we also use Google Analytics 4, a service from Google, to measure how
      visitors use the site. The Google Analytics script does not load until you accept. Once you accept, Google
      Analytics sets cookies named _ga and _ga_ followed by an ID, which normally last up to two years, and collects
      information such as pages viewed, time on page, referring site, browser and device type and approximate
      location. We turn off Google signals and ad personalisation for analytics. If you press Reject or make no choice,
      Google Analytics does not load. You can change your choice at any time with the Cookie choices link in the footer.
      You can also install the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt out browser add on</a>.
      See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Hosting</h3>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub states that when a GitHub Pages site is visited, the visitor's IP
      address is logged and stored for security purposes. We do not receive or control those logs. See the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its advertising partners use cookies and similar
      technologies to serve and measure ads, including ads based on your earlier visits to this and other sites. You
      can learn how Google uses data from sites that use its services, and manage your ad settings, at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>.
      Visitors in the European Union and the United Kingdom see a consent choice delivered by Google, and you can
      change that choice at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and affiliate tracking</h2>
    <p>
      Apart from the cookies set by Google for advertising and the Google Analytics cookies set only if you accept them, this site does not set cookies of its own. We store your cookie choice in your browser's local storage. We do not
      currently run affiliate tracking. Booking buttons currently open an internal placeholder page, not a partner
      site. If we add affiliate links in future, we will update this policy and our
      <a href="/disclosure/">Affiliate disclosure</a> before they go live.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use your data</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>To answer messages you send us, based on your request and our legitimate interest in replying.</li>
      <li>To understand overall site usage and keep the site working and secure, based on our legitimate interests.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell or rent personal data. Data is handled by the service providers named above (FormSubmit, Google,
      Cloudflare and GitHub) only as needed to provide their services. We may disclose data if the law requires it.
      These providers may process data in the United States and other countries.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep contact messages only as long as needed to handle your request and for ordinary business records, then
      delete them. Analytics data is shown to us only in aggregated form.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to tell you what personal data we hold about you, correct it or delete it by emailing
      <a href="mailto:joshuaofisrael@gmail.com">joshuaofisrael@gmail.com</a>. Depending on where you live, you may have
      further rights, including the right to complain to your local data protection authority. You can block the
      analytics script with your browser or a content blocker and the site will still work.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal data.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      This page is governed by the laws of the State of Florida, and any dispute will be heard in the state or federal
      courts located in Florida. Pick Your Row is owned and operated by Joshua Israel Ventures LLC, a Florida limited
      liability company.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>, <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> and
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>
    <p class="muted legal-ownership">© 2026 Joshua Israel Ventures LLC. All rights reserved. Pick Your Row is a trade name of Joshua Israel Ventures LLC, a Florida limited liability company.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
